ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">These events do not establish a class-=
wide toxicity. They will nevertheless increase scrutiny of cell-expansion kin=
etics, dose, lymphodepletion, patient selection, inflammatory biomarkers and =
whether rheumatology or neurology sites can recognize and manage delayed immu=
ne complications.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What to watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Whether the events cluster by indicati=
on, protocol or manufacturing design; regulatory requirements for restarting =
the studies; and whether competing programs alter dosing or monitoring proact=
ively.</p>
<h4 style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;color:#1=
2395b;margin:16px 0 6px;">Camizestrant makes serial liquid biopsy part of tre=
atment=E2=80=94not merely diagnosis</h4>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What changed</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">FDA granted accelerated approval to As=
traZeneca=E2=80=99s oral SERD camizestrant with a continuing CDK4/6 inhibitor=
 when Guardant360 CDx detects an emerging ESR1 mutation during aromatase-inhi=
bitor/CDK4/6 therapy, before radiographic progression. In the 315-patient SER=
ENA-6 trial, median progression-free survival was 16.0 months versus 9.2 mont=
hs for continued aromatase inhibition, a 56% reduction in progression or deat=
h risk. (<a href=3D"https://www.fda.gov/drugs/resources-information-approved-=
drugs/fda-grants-accelerated-approval-camizestrant-cdk46-inhibitor-esr1-mutat=
ed-hr-positive-her2-negative?utm_source=3Dopenai" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text=
-decoration:underline;">fda.gov</a>)</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What it tells us</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The strategic advance is broader than =
another endocrine drug. FDA has endorsed longitudinal molecular surveillance =
as a trigger for changing treatment while the patient remains clinically and =
radiographically stable. That creates recurring diagnostic demand and could e=
xtend first-line CDK4/6 use while displacing some post-progression therapy.</=
p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The unresolved question is whether ear=
lier switching improves survival or primarily shifts the treatment clock forw=
ard, exposing patients to a new drug=E2=80=94and payers to additional cost=E2=
=80=94sooner.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;"><strong>What to watch next</strong></p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Overall-survival maturation, confirmat=
ory requirements, adherence to serial ctDNA testing and payer policies govern=
ing testing frequency.</p>
<h4 style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;color:#1=
2395b;margin:16px 0 6px;">Etentamig and ivonescimab pressure incumbents throu=
gh different forms of differentiation</h4>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">AbbVie=E2=80=99s Phase 3 CERVINO trial=
 showed a 74.0% response rate for BCMA=C3=97CD3 bispecific etentamig versus 4=
5.7% with standard regimens, with a PFS hazard ratio of 0.40. Grade 3/4 infec=
tions remained substantial at 27.7%, but cytokine-release syndrome was predom=
inantly grade 1, with no grade 3 or higher events reported. Monthly dosing be=
gan after a single step-up dose. (<a href=3D"https://news.abbvie.com/2026-09-=
03-AbbVie-Announces-Positive-Topline-Results-from-the-Phase-3-CERVINO-Trial-S=
howing-Etentamig-Significantly-Improved-Response-Rate-and-Progression-Free-Su=
rvival-in-Patients-with-Relapsed-Refractory-Multiple-Myeloma?utm_source=3Dope=
nai" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">news.abbvie.com</a>)<=
/p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">The value proposition is therefore not=
 simply another active BCMA therapy. A manageable initiation process and mont=
hly schedule could move treatment beyond specialized centers, expanding the e=
conomically reachable market even without demonstrating superior efficacy to =
another BCMA bispecific.</p>
<p style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-heig=
ht:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 12px;">Separately, ivonescimab monotherapy ac=
hieved statistically significant overall survival versus pembrolizumab in PD-=
L1-positive first-line NSCLC in China. Coming one week after its biliary-trac=
t survival win, the result further strengthens the PD-1/VEGF architecture; ho=
wever, undisclosed effect sizes and the China-only population leave global di=
fferentiation unresolved. Summit=E2=80=99s U.S. decision for a different EGFR=
-mutant indication is due November 14. (<a href=3D"https://smmttx.com/news/pr=
ess-releases/news-details/2026/Ivonescimab-Monotherapy-Demonstrates-Statistic=
ally-Significant-Overall-Survival-Benefit-Compared-to-Pembrolizumab-Monothera=
py-in-PD-L1-Positive-Advanced-NSCLC-in-HARMONi-2-Study-Conducted-by-Akeso-in-=
China/default.aspx" style=3D"color:#1a5e9a;text-decoration:underline;">smmttx=
.com</a>)</p>
<h3 style=3D"font-family:Georgia, 'Times New Roman', serif;font-size:17px;col=
or:#12395b;margin:22px 0 8px;">Additional Strategic Signals</h3>
<ul style=3D"margin:0 0 12px;padding-left:22px;">
<li style=3D"font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:15px;line-hei=
ght:1.5;color:#1f2933;margin:0 0 6px;"><strong>Rare neurological ASOs diverge=
